exts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Someone's Feelings and Reactions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You talk about feelings and reactions using adjectives.<br/><br/>Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> are used to describe how a person feels, like <span class=\"italic\">annoyed, fascinated, entertained, surprised, worried</span> or <span class =\"italic\">tired</span>.<br/><br/>Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ing</span> are used to describe things and situations, like <span class =\"italic\">annoying, entertaining, surprising, worrying</span> or <span class =\"italic\">tiring</span>.  <br/>These adjectives describe the <span class =\"italic\">effect</span> something has on a person.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " The results of the test can be surprising or even shocking.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are you excited about the idea of challenge? Do you feel annoyed when people disagree with you?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Speculating about Feelings and Impressions  ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you speculate about something, you are making a guess based on what you know about the situation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can show you are speculating about something by using a modal, like <span class =\"italic\">must</span> or <span class =\"italic\">can't</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The modal is followed by a verb in the base form. You do not use \u201cto\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These are formal structures.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Personality tests are very popular. People must enjoy thinking about their personality.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The Myers-Briggs test separates people into 16 well-defined categories. In my opinion, that can't always be the case. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shocking", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very surprising, to the point of feeling shocked", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  The results of personality tests can be surprising or even shocking.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about personality.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "entertaining", "type": "name"}, {"content": "fun; amusing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Whatever you think about the results of your tests, it's entertaining to talk about personality.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "well-defined", "type": "name"}, {"content": "definite; separate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Myers-Briggs test separates people into 16 well-defined categories. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "annoyed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling unhappy; irritated", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you feel annoyed when people disagree with you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "executive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the person responsible for a company", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If so, you must be the Executive type.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "attribute", 