out\nhow a person makes decisions, the way in which they communicate, as well as their general\nattitude. This information can then be used to select the best employee for a certain\nproject or task.", "time": "29000"}, {"image": "engenn7le02ob05re2img06.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "The Myers-Briggs test separates people into 16 well-defined categories. In my\nopinion, that can't always be the case. Are you excited about the idea of\nchallenge? Do you feel annoyed when people disagree with you? If so, you must be\nthe Executive type. Are you worried about what people think? Are social\nsituations somewhat frustrating to you? You must fall into the Artist type. Whatever you think\nabout the results of your tests, it's entertaining to talk about personality.", "time": "45000"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le02ob05re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": ""}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}]}